  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "Sidewalk Stewards is a visual analytics platform designed to clean topological errors in aerial-extracted sidewalk networks by flagging anomalies like disconnected components, dangling edges, and malformed intersections. The system combines coordinated spatial views for manual correction with live routing and accessibility metric updates. In comparative user tests, case studies across multiple cities, and quantitative evaluations, the interface allowed users to find and fix errors faster than standard workflows, with a minor volume of manual edits yielding broad spatial graph quality improvements.",
      "why": "It replaces brute-force manual editing with an interactive, semi-automated process, turning imperfect computer vision outputs into routing-ready spatial networks for municipal accessibility planning."
    }
